{"ref":"BDB, אַיָּלוֹן","hw":"אַיָּלוֹן","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">אַיָּלוֹן</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.loc. (</strong><em>Deer</em>-field<strong>) Aijalon</strong>—<span dir=\"rtl\">א׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 10:12\" href=\"/Joshua.10.12\">Jos 10:12</a> + 8 times; <span dir=\"rtl\">אַיָּלֹ֫נָה</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 14:31\" href=\"/I_Samuel.14.31\">1 S 14:31</a>—<br><strong>1.</strong>  city in Dan <a data-ref=\"Joshua 19:42\" href=\"/Joshua.19.42\">Jos 19:42</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 21:24\" href=\"/Joshua.21.24\">21:24</a> (Levit. city) <a data-ref=\"Judges 1:35\" href=\"/Judges.1.35\">Ju 1:35</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 14:31\" href=\"/I_Samuel.14.31\">1 S 14:31</a> doubtless same; so <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 6:54\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.6.54\">1 Ch 6:54</a> (where Dan om.); app. later in Benj. <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 8:13\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.8.13\">1 Ch 8:13</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 11:10\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.11.10\">2 Ch 11:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 28:18\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.28.18\">28:18</a> (v. Be); <span dir=\"rtl\">עֵמֶק אַיָּלוֹן</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 10:12\" href=\"/Joshua.10.12\">Jos 10:12</a> almost certainly named from same; = Epiph. Ἰαλω, mod. <em>Jâlo</em> Rob<sup>BR ii. 253</sup>, Survey<sup>iii. 19</sup>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  city in Zebulun <a data-ref=\"Judges 12:12\" href=\"/Judges.12.12\">Ju 12:12</a>.","next":"BDB, אוּלַי","prev":"BDB, אַיָּלָה"}